            <div xml:id="d303-a10">

                <pb facs="0367" n="1101" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1101"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure to inclosure
                    9.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Examining Magistrate to Mr. Rawicz.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Examining Magistrate of the Warsaw Court of Justice, Ministry of
                                Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Nieszawa
                            District</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-09-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1632.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">To the Consul of the United States of America, N. D.
                        83–95:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In reply to your dispatch of September 2, No. 1530,1 have the honor to inform you
                    that Anton Yablkowski had to deliver to the police his passport given to him at
                    Washington, December 7, 1894, No. 18144, because Anton Yablkowski is a Russian
                    subject, incorporated to the village Palaevo St rave, Rushkaw gnun (?), of the
                    Nieszawa district; and, on the strength of his having passed over to a foreign
                    subjection, the said Anton Yablkowski will be tried according to article 325 of
                    the Code of Laws.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
